    "updated_at": "2024-06-18T09:06:03Z",
    "body": "> This PR does not handle dismiss yet?\r\n\r\nWell it does, on the assumption that none/accept/dismiss are the only available options. In that case \"dismiss\" is what happens when the return value is neither \"none\" nor \"accept\". I think for `beforeUnload` it needs some changes to make the behavior well-defined (we set a variable inside a conditional and later assume it has a value)",
